 ## Threats to validity
 
-* Five small, synthetic defects in one TypeScript service; the defects were written alongside the
-  system that solves them.
-* The mock comparison is constructed; only a real-model run measures the method.
-* Single run per configuration; real models are stochastic — repeat runs (`n ≥ 5`) are needed for
-  rates with confidence intervals.
+* Ten defects, nine of them planted in one small TypeScript service by the people who built the
+  system that solves them. Only R1 is a real bug in someone else's code.
+* Three repeats per configuration: enough to see that the D6 difference is not a one-off, not
+  enough for tight confidence intervals.
+* Muse Spark 1.3 fixed most defects in one shot; the set does not yet contain defects hard enough
+  to separate Baseline C from FORGE-0 on fix rate.
 * The hidden tests are stricter than the visible tests but not exhaustive.
+* The offline sandbox does not install dependencies, so only projects whose tests run on Node's
+  built-in runner or on pytest with the standard library can be evaluated.
